  "result": "Perfect! All 113 tests pass. Here's a summary of the VAT implementation:\n\n## Changes Made:\n\n### 1. **Added `lineVat()` function** (`src/invoices.js`)\n   - Calculates VAT per line on the amount after discount\n   - VAT formula: (lineTotal - discount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100\n   - Rounds result to whole cents\n\n### 2. **Updated `invoiceTotals()`** to include VAT\n   - Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n   - VAT is the sum of all line VATs (not a percentage of invoice total)\n   - Total = subtotal - discount + vat (all clamped at 0)\n\n### 3. **Updated `renderInvoiceText()`** to display VAT\n   - Shows VAT line only when VAT > 0\n   - VAT line appears just above the total\n   - Example output:\n     ```\n     DRAFT\n     Company Name\n     2 Item @ \u20ac50.00 = \u20ac100.00\n     VAT: \u20ac21.00\n     Total: \u20ac121.00\n     ```\n\n### 4. **Added 13 new VAT tests**\n   - Tests for `lineVat()` calculation with different rates (21%, 9%, 0%)\n   - Tests for VAT with discounts applied\n   - Tests for proper rounding of fractional VAT amounts\n   - Tests for VAT rendering in invoice text\n   - Tests confirming VAT line only shows when VAT > 0\n\n### Key Features:\n- \u2705 VAT calculated per line after discount is applied\n- \u2705 Fractional VAT amounts rounded to whole cents per line\n- \u2705 Invoice VAT is sum of line VATs, not a percentage of total\n- \u2705 All amounts properly formatted and clamped at 0\n- \u2705 Clean rendering with VAT displayed separately from total\n\n**Test Results**: \u2705 All 113 tests pass",
